WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.011
This, that, these, those.

2
00:00:02.361 --> 00:00:05.068
A pointing word shows which
thing or person you mean.

3
00:00:05.168 --> 00:00:07.884
It is fixed. Its last
letter never changes.

4
00:00:08.334 --> 00:00:10.342
Chapter one. The table to learn.

5
00:00:10.592 --> 00:00:13.976
Arabic has a word for near
things and a word for far things.

6
00:00:14.076 --> 00:00:16.846
Each one also changes for
male, female and plural.

7
00:00:17.296 --> 00:00:19.100
Read the table one row at a time.

8
00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:20.762
The first row is near.

9
00:00:21.012 --> 00:00:22.522
One male or thing: this.

10
00:00:22.772 --> 00:00:23.604
‫هَذَا‬

11
00:00:23.854 --> 00:00:25.540
One female or thing: this.

12
00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:26.684
‫هَذِهِ‬

13
00:00:26.934 --> 00:00:28.469
A group of people: these.

14
00:00:28.719 --> 00:00:29.980
‫هَؤُلَاءِ‬

15
00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:31.766
The second row is far.

16
00:00:32.016 --> 00:00:33.505
One male or thing: that.

17
00:00:33.755 --> 00:00:34.654
‫ذَلِكَ‬

18
00:00:34.904 --> 00:00:36.379
One female or thing: that.

19
00:00:36.629 --> 00:00:37.387
‫تِلْكَ‬

20
00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:39.157
A group of people: those.

21
00:00:39.407 --> 00:00:40.540
‫أُولَئِكَ‬

22
00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:42.807
Learn these six words by heart.

23
00:00:43.257 --> 00:00:44.858
Two more words. Here.

24
00:00:45.108 --> 00:00:45.898
‫هُنَا‬

25
00:00:46.148 --> 00:00:46.899
And there.

26
00:00:47.049 --> 00:00:47.914
‫هُنَاكَ‬

27
00:00:48.364 --> 00:00:50.199
These two words point to a place.

28
00:00:50.449 --> 00:00:53.646
Madinah lesson 5: It is
under the desk, over there.

29
00:00:53.896 --> 00:00:56.699
‫هُوَ تَحْتَ الْمَكْتَبِ هُنَاكَ‬

30
00:00:57.149 --> 00:00:58.793
Learn the last vowel too.

31
00:00:59.043 --> 00:01:00.581
The first word ends in alif.

32
00:01:00.831 --> 00:01:01.663
‫هَذَا‬

33
00:01:01.913 --> 00:01:03.399
Two words end in kasra.

34
00:01:03.649 --> 00:01:04.543
‫هَذِهِ‬

35
00:01:04.793 --> 00:01:06.054
‫هَؤُلَاءِ‬

36
00:01:06.304 --> 00:01:07.787
Four words end in fatha.

37
00:01:08.037 --> 00:01:08.936
‫ذَلِكَ‬

38
00:01:09.186 --> 00:01:09.944
‫تِلْكَ‬

39
00:01:10.194 --> 00:01:11.327
‫أُولَئِكَ‬

40
00:01:11.577 --> 00:01:12.442
‫هُنَاكَ‬

41
00:01:12.892 --> 00:01:14.512
These endings never change.

42
00:01:14.762 --> 00:01:16.600
The kasra is not a sign of jarr.

43
00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:18.521
The fatha is not a sign of naṣb.

44
00:01:18.971 --> 00:01:19.661
A tip.

45
00:01:19.911 --> 00:01:21.172
‫هَؤُلَاءِ‬

46
00:01:21.322 --> 00:01:22.455
‫أُولَئِكَ‬

47
00:01:22.705 --> 00:01:25.389
These two are for groups
of people, male or female.

48
00:01:25.489 --> 00:01:26.589
These are students.

49
00:01:26.739 --> 00:01:28.788
‫هَؤُلَاءِ طُلَّابٌ‬

50
00:01:29.038 --> 00:01:29.956
These are women.

51
00:01:30.106 --> 00:01:32.106
‫هَؤُلَاءِ نِسَاءٌ‬

52
00:01:32.556 --> 00:01:35.444
For plural things, Arabic
normally uses this word.

53
00:01:35.694 --> 00:01:36.588
‫هَذِهِ‬

54
00:01:36.838 --> 00:01:37.848
These are books.

55
00:01:37.998 --> 00:01:39.530
‫هَذِهِ كُتُبٌ‬

56
00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:45.214
Chapter two. Reading tips:
hidden and extra letters.

57
00:01:45.464 --> 00:01:48.944
Some pointing words are not read
exactly as they are written.

58
00:01:49.044 --> 00:01:51.989
The Qur'an shows the hidden
alif with a small alif on top.

59
00:01:52.239 --> 00:01:53.071
‫هٰذَا‬

60
00:01:53.521 --> 00:01:55.372
Listen to how each word is said.

61
00:01:55.622 --> 00:01:56.454
‫هَذَا‬

62
00:01:56.704 --> 00:02:00.177
A long alif sound after the letter
ha is said, but not written.

63
00:02:00.427 --> 00:02:01.382
The next word.

64
00:02:01.532 --> 00:02:02.426
‫هَذِهِ‬

65
00:02:02.676 --> 00:02:04.247
The same hidden sound after ha.

66
00:02:04.497 --> 00:02:05.405
And this one.

67
00:02:05.555 --> 00:02:06.816
‫هَؤُلَاءِ‬

68
00:02:07.066 --> 00:02:08.637
The same hidden sound after ha.

69
00:02:08.887 --> 00:02:09.900
Now a far word.

70
00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:11.049
‫ذَلِكَ‬

71
00:02:11.299 --> 00:02:14.303
A long alif sound after dhal
is said, but not written.

72
00:02:14.553 --> 00:02:16.408
The last word has two surprises.

73
00:02:16.658 --> 00:02:17.791
‫أُولَئِكَ‬

74
00:02:18.041 --> 00:02:20.052
The letter waw is written, but not read.

75
00:02:20.152 --> 00:02:23.384
And a long alif sound after
lam is said, but not written.

76
00:02:23.834 --> 00:02:26.437
A tip. Do not write the
hidden alif yourself.

77
00:02:26.687 --> 00:02:28.488
These two have the alif written in.

78
00:02:28.588 --> 00:02:30.046
They are spelling mistakes.

79
00:02:30.496 --> 00:02:33.213
Chapter three. This is
a book, or this book?

80
00:02:33.463 --> 00:02:35.439
Look at the noun after the pointing word.

81
00:02:35.539 --> 00:02:36.495
Does it have al?

82
00:02:36.945 --> 00:02:38.280
No al: a sentence.

83
00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:39.418
This is a book.

84
00:02:39.668 --> 00:02:41.098
‫هَذَا كِتَابٌ‬

85
00:02:41.548 --> 00:02:43.244
The pointing word is the Topic.

86
00:02:43.344 --> 00:02:45.158
The noun, book, is the Information.

87
00:02:45.508 --> 00:02:46.716
With al: a phrase.

88
00:02:46.816 --> 00:02:47.561
This book.

89
00:02:47.711 --> 00:02:49.225
‫هَذَا الْكِتَابُ‬

90
00:02:49.475 --> 00:02:52.014
It is not finished yet. Add Information.

91
00:02:52.114 --> 00:02:53.290
This book is new.

92
00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:55.866
‫هَذَا الْكِتَابُ جَدِيدٌ‬

93
00:02:56.316 --> 00:02:57.485
This is a house.

94
00:02:57.735 --> 00:02:59.198
‫هَذَا بَيْتٌ‬

95
00:02:59.448 --> 00:03:00.476
A full sentence.

96
00:03:00.826 --> 00:03:02.042
This house is near.

97
00:03:02.292 --> 00:03:04.606
‫هَذَا الْبَيْتُ قَرِيبٌ‬

98
00:03:04.856 --> 00:03:06.436
‫هَذَا الْبَيْتُ‬

99
00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:08.006
It is the Topic part.

100
00:03:08.256 --> 00:03:09.118
‫قَرِيبٌ‬

101
00:03:09.368 --> 00:03:10.647
It is the Information.

102
00:03:10.997 --> 00:03:11.970
That is a car.

103
00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:13.744
‫تِلْكَ سَيَّارَةٌ‬

104
00:03:13.994 --> 00:03:15.022
A full sentence.

105
00:03:15.372 --> 00:03:16.504
That car is new.

106
00:03:16.754 --> 00:03:19.499
‫تِلْكَ السَّيَّارَةُ جَدِيدَةٌ‬

107
00:03:19.749 --> 00:03:21.534
‫تِلْكَ السَّيَّارَةُ‬

108
00:03:21.784 --> 00:03:23.047
It means that car.

109
00:03:23.497 --> 00:03:25.776
A tip. How do you say: this is the book?

110
00:03:26.226 --> 00:03:28.170
Put the word for he or she in the middle.

111
00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:29.241
‫هُوَ‬

112
00:03:29.391 --> 00:03:30.072
‫هِيَ‬

113
00:03:30.322 --> 00:03:31.485
This is the book.

114
00:03:31.735 --> 00:03:33.643
‫هَذَا هُوَ الْكِتَابُ‬

115
00:03:33.893 --> 00:03:35.045
This is the watch.

116
00:03:35.295 --> 00:03:37.565
‫هَذِهِ هِيَ السَّاعَةُ‬

117
00:03:38.015 --> 00:03:42.233
Another tip. A noun in iḍāfa has
no al, so it makes a sentence.

118
00:03:42.333 --> 00:03:45.332
From Madinah lesson 5:
This is Hamid's house.

119
00:03:45.582 --> 00:03:47.233
‫هَذَا بَيْتُ حَامِدٍ‬

120
00:03:49.367 --> 00:03:51.277
Chapter four. Follow the noun.

121
00:03:51.527 --> 00:03:53.979
Choose the pointing word
by the noun you point to.

122
00:03:54.229 --> 00:03:55.400
Is it near or far?

123
00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:56.796
Male or female?

124
00:03:57.146 --> 00:03:58.729
One, or a group of people?

125
00:03:59.179 --> 00:04:01.152
This is a pen, and this is a watch.

126
00:04:01.402 --> 00:04:04.700
‫هَذَا قَلَمٌ وَهَذِهِ سَاعَةٌ‬

127
00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:05.715
‫قَلَمٌ‬

128
00:04:05.965 --> 00:04:07.120
It is masculine.

129
00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:08.214
‫سَاعَةٌ‬

130
00:04:08.464 --> 00:04:09.416
It is feminine.

131
00:04:09.766 --> 00:04:11.843
That is a mosque, and that is a school.

132
00:04:12.093 --> 00:04:15.614
‫ذَلِكَ مَسْجِدٌ وَتِلْكَ مَدْرَسَةٌ‬

133
00:04:15.864 --> 00:04:16.837
Both are far.

134
00:04:16.987 --> 00:04:18.027
For masculine:

135
00:04:18.277 --> 00:04:19.176
‫ذَلِكَ‬

136
00:04:19.426 --> 00:04:20.417
For feminine:

137
00:04:20.667 --> 00:04:21.425
‫تِلْكَ‬

138
00:04:21.675 --> 00:04:23.706
These are students, and those are men.

139
00:04:23.956 --> 00:04:28.124
‫هَؤُلَاءِ طُلَّابٌ وَأُولَئِكَ رِجَالٌ‬

140
00:04:28.374 --> 00:04:29.513
Groups of people.

141
00:04:29.663 --> 00:04:30.924
‫هَؤُلَاءِ‬

142
00:04:31.174 --> 00:04:32.307
‫أُولَئِكَ‬

143
00:04:32.557 --> 00:04:33.599
This is a girl.

144
00:04:33.849 --> 00:04:35.579
‫هَذِهِ بِنْتٌ‬

145
00:04:35.829 --> 00:04:36.746
‫بِنْتٌ‬

146
00:04:36.996 --> 00:04:39.227
It has no ta marbuta, but it is feminine.

147
00:04:39.327 --> 00:04:40.627
So we use this word.

148
00:04:40.877 --> 00:04:41.771
‫هَذِهِ‬

149
00:04:42.221 --> 00:04:44.562
Chapter five. Its place in the sentence.

150
00:04:44.812 --> 00:04:47.525
A pointing word is fixed,
but it still has a job.

151
00:04:47.625 --> 00:04:49.152
The job gives it a place.

152
00:04:49.252 --> 00:04:52.883
The noun after it shows the ending
that the pointing word cannot show.

153
00:04:53.333 --> 00:04:54.371
This is a book.

154
00:04:54.621 --> 00:04:56.051
‫هَذَا كِتَابٌ‬

155
00:04:56.301 --> 00:04:57.133
‫هَذَا‬

156
00:04:57.383 --> 00:05:00.457
It is the Topic. It is
fixed, in the place of rafʿ.

157
00:05:00.807 --> 00:05:02.391
This man entered the mosque.

158
00:05:02.641 --> 00:05:05.830
‫دَخَلَ هَذَا الرَّجُلُ الْمَسْجِدَ‬

159
00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:06.912
‫هَذَا‬

160
00:05:07.162 --> 00:05:11.453
It is the doer. Place of rafʿ. See
the damma on the noun after it.

161
00:05:11.703 --> 00:05:12.689
‫الرَّجُلُ‬

162
00:05:12.939 --> 00:05:14.409
The student opened this door.

163
00:05:14.659 --> 00:05:17.633
‫فَتَحَ الطَّالِبُ هَذَا الْبَابَ‬

164
00:05:17.883 --> 00:05:18.715
‫هَذَا‬

165
00:05:18.965 --> 00:05:23.337
It is the object. Place of naṣb.
See the fatha on the noun after it.

166
00:05:23.587 --> 00:05:24.527
‫الْبَابَ‬

167
00:05:24.777 --> 00:05:25.767
In this house.

168
00:05:25.917 --> 00:05:27.902
‫فِي هَذَا الْبَيْتِ‬

169
00:05:28.152 --> 00:05:28.984
‫هَذَا‬

170
00:05:29.234 --> 00:05:34.321
It comes after a preposition. Place of
jarr. The noun after it shows the kasra.

171
00:05:34.571 --> 00:05:35.539
‫الْبَيْتِ‬

172
00:05:35.789 --> 00:05:37.028
This student's book.

173
00:05:37.178 --> 00:05:39.801
‫كِتَابُ هَذَا الطَّالِبِ‬

174
00:05:40.051 --> 00:05:40.883
‫هَذَا‬

175
00:05:41.133 --> 00:05:43.087
It is the owner. Place of jarr.

176
00:05:43.537 --> 00:05:45.825
So a pointing word has
one of three places.

177
00:05:46.075 --> 00:05:47.028
Place of rafʿ.

178
00:05:47.178 --> 00:05:49.518
‫فِي مَحَلِّ رَفْعٍ‬

179
00:05:49.768 --> 00:05:51.976
For the Topic, the
Information and the doer.

180
00:05:52.326 --> 00:05:53.281
Place of naṣb.

181
00:05:53.431 --> 00:05:55.574
‫فِي مَحَلِّ نَصْبٍ‬

182
00:05:55.824 --> 00:05:57.934
For the object, and the other naṣb jobs.

183
00:05:58.284 --> 00:05:59.238
Place of jarr.

184
00:05:59.388 --> 00:06:01.509
‫فِي مَحَلِّ جَرٍّ‬

185
00:06:01.759 --> 00:06:03.829
After a preposition, or for the owner.

186
00:06:05.967 --> 00:06:08.656
Chapter six. Two words that are not fixed.

187
00:06:09.106 --> 00:06:11.946
Look at the words that mean
these two. They change.

188
00:06:12.196 --> 00:06:13.199
For two males.

189
00:06:13.349 --> 00:06:14.375
‫هَذَانِ‬

190
00:06:14.625 --> 00:06:15.674
For two females.

191
00:06:15.824 --> 00:06:16.865
‫هَاتَانِ‬

192
00:06:17.115 --> 00:06:18.437
Both words are flexible.

193
00:06:18.537 --> 00:06:20.298
In naṣb and jarr, they become:

194
00:06:20.548 --> 00:06:21.543
‫هَذَيْنِ‬

195
00:06:21.793 --> 00:06:22.781
‫هَاتَيْنِ‬

196
00:06:23.031 --> 00:06:25.277
You learn them with the dual in Stage 4.

197
00:06:25.727 --> 00:06:26.506
In rafʿ.

198
00:06:26.656 --> 00:06:27.682
‫هَذَانِ‬

199
00:06:27.932 --> 00:06:28.973
‫هَاتَانِ‬

200
00:06:29.223 --> 00:06:30.489
In naṣb and jarr.

201
00:06:30.739 --> 00:06:31.734
‫هَذَيْنِ‬

202
00:06:31.984 --> 00:06:32.972
‫هَاتَيْنِ‬

203
00:06:33.422 --> 00:06:34.274
In short.

204
00:06:34.524 --> 00:06:35.140
One. Near.

205
00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:36.122
‫هَذَا‬

206
00:06:36.272 --> 00:06:37.166
‫هَذِهِ‬

207
00:06:37.316 --> 00:06:38.577
‫هَؤُلَاءِ‬

208
00:06:38.827 --> 00:06:39.510
Far.

209
00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:40.559
‫ذَلِكَ‬

210
00:06:40.709 --> 00:06:41.467
‫تِلْكَ‬

211
00:06:41.617 --> 00:06:42.750
‫أُولَئِكَ‬

212
00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:43.724
Place.

213
00:06:43.874 --> 00:06:44.664
‫هُنَا‬

214
00:06:44.814 --> 00:06:45.679
‫هُنَاكَ‬

215
00:06:45.929 --> 00:06:47.508
Two. Choose by the noun.

216
00:06:47.658 --> 00:06:50.747
Near or far, male or female,
one or a group of people.

217
00:06:51.097 --> 00:06:51.787
Three.

218
00:06:51.937 --> 00:06:53.367
‫هَذَا كِتَابٌ‬

219
00:06:53.617 --> 00:06:54.844
That is a sentence.

220
00:06:55.094 --> 00:06:56.608
‫هَذَا الْكِتَابُ‬

221
00:06:56.858 --> 00:06:58.540
That is a phrase: this book.

222
00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:03.684
Four. Pointing words are fixed, but
they have a place. Rafʿ, naṣb or jarr.

223
00:07:04.034 --> 00:07:04.742
Five.

224
00:07:04.892 --> 00:07:05.918
‫هَذَانِ‬

225
00:07:06.068 --> 00:07:07.109
‫هَاتَانِ‬

226
00:07:07.359 --> 00:07:10.050
They are not fixed. They wait for Stage 4.

227
00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:13.134
Now it is your turn.
Open the Practice tab.

228
00:07:13.234 --> 00:07:15.182
Do the six cards, then the homework.
